$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 2-Amino-2'-nitro Diphenylsulfide (IIIa). 2-Aminobenzenethiol
Ia (0.1 m ole) was dissolved in ethanol (20 niL) containing 0.1 mole of
anhydrous sodium acetate in 50 niL round bottom flask and
halonitrobenzene IIa (0.1 m ole) in 10 mL ethanol was added. The reaction
mixture was refluxed for 4-5 hours and concentrated in an ice bath
overnight. The solid that separated out was filtered, washed with 30%
ethanol, and recrystallized from methanol. Yield: 85%. m.p.: 108 °C,
Molecular formula: C12H8N2O2SFCl, % found(calcd.) C: 48.02 (48.24), H:
2.66 (2.68), N: 9.36 (9.38).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, regioselective
