$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-Bromo-4-acetyl-1-((4-methoxyphenyl)sulfinyl)benzene 1f A mixture of
1-bromo-2-fluoro-5-acetyl-benzene (1.5 g, 7.1 mmol),
4-methoxybenzenethiol (0.9 g, 7.0 mmol), K2CO3 (1.1 g, 7.9 mmol) in DMF
(5 mL) was heated to 160 ◦C for 2 h in a closed vial. After cooling to
ambient temperature the mixture was diluted with diethyl ether (10 mL),
washed (water, brine), dried (MgSO4) and concentrated in vaccuo.
Purrification by column chromatography (solvent: c-hexane : ethyl acetate
= 2 : 1) afforded the corresponding thioether. dark red oil (1.2 g, 5.9
mmol, 84 %). 1H-NMR (CDCl3, 300MHz): δ= 8.04 (d, J = 1.3Hz, 1H), 7.60
(dd, J = 8.4, 1.3Hz, 1H), 7.46 (d, J = 8.4Hz, 2H), 6.97 (d,J = 8.4Hz,
2H), 6.61 (d, J = 8.4Hz, 1H), 3.84 (s, 3H), 2.49 (s, 3H) ppm. 13C-NMR
(CDCl3, 75MHz): δ= 195.8, 161.1, 148.2, 137.5, 134.7, 132.4, 127.1,
125.9, 120.4, 119.6, 115.7, 55.4, 26.3 ppm. MS (EI): m/z = 336.0, 338.0.
IR (ATR): ev = 2929 (w), 1669 (s), 1581 (s), 1381 (s), 1225 (s) cm-1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM closed vial used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Palladium-Catalyzed Intramolecular Direct Arylation of 2-Bromo-diaryl
Sulfoxides via C-H Bond Activation
