$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthetic Procedure of 4,4'-Bis(p-tolylthio)biphenyl (3b). To a solution
of Pd(OAc)2 (4.5 mg, 4 mol %) and Xantphos (12.1 mg, 4.2 mol %) in DMF
(1.0 mL) was added 4,4'-dibromo-1,1'-biphenyl (156 mg, 0.5 mmol) in DMF
(0.5 mL) at 25 °C under nitrogen atmosphere. After being stirred for 5
min, (4-Me-C6H4S)3In (164.7 mg, 0.34 mmol) and DIPEA (87.0 μL, 0.5 mmol)
in DMF (1.0 mL) was transferred via double-ended needle, and the mixture
was stirred at 100 °C for 4 h. The reaction mixture was quenched with
NaHCO3 (satd aq). The aqueous layer was extracted with ether (3x20 mL),
and the combined organic layers were washed with water and brine, dried
with MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated under reduced pressure. The
residue was purified by silica gel column chromatography to give 3b
(167.4 mg, 84%) as white solid. 4,4'-Bis(p-tolylthio)biphenyl (3b), yield
(167.4 mg, 84%) mp 159 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.45 (d, J = 8.36Hz,
2H), 7.34 (d, J = 8.00Hz, 2H), 7.30 (d, J = 8.36Hz, 2H), 7.16 (d, J =
8.00Hz, 2H), 2.35 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 138.9, 138.2,
136.9, 132.9, 131.4, 130.6, 130.3, 127.8, 21.6; IR (film) 3431, 809 cm-1;
HRMS (EI) calcd for C26H22S2 m/z 398.1163 [M+], found m/z 398.1164.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Di-, Tri-, and Tetrasulfides through Multifold Carbon-Sulfur
Cross-Coupling Reactions with Indium Tri(organothiolates) in a One-Pot
Procedure
