$DATUM (3,5-Dimethoxyphenyl)(2,6-dimethylphenyl)sulfide S3.
Tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium (23 mg, 0.02 mmol), (S)-BINAP (25
mg, 0,04 mmol), potassium hydroxide (0.45 g, 8.00 mmol) and
3,5-dimethoxybromobenzene (0.87 g, 4.00 mmol) were added to a
metal-capped test tube with Teflon-lined septum. The tube was evacuated
and backfilled with argon (3 cycles). 2-Propanol (3.6 mL) and
2,6-dimethylbenzenethiol (0.53 mL, 4.00 mmoL) were added at room
temperature. The tube was heated to 80 °C and stirred for 24 h. The
reaction mixture was then allowed to cool to room temperature before the
addition of aqueous saturated NH4Cl (2 mL). The aqueous layer was then
extracted with EtOAc (3 X 5 mL) and the combined organic layer washed
with brine (5 mL), dried (Na2SO4) and concentrated in vacuo. The crude
product was purified by column chromatography on silica gel eluting with
100:1 n-hexane/EtOAc to yield the product (0.92 g, 84% yield) as a
colourless oil; (3,5-Dimethoxyphenyl)(2,6-dimethylphenyl)sulfide S3. 0.92
g, 84% yield. νmax (neat)/cm-1 3054, 3012, 3001, 2948, 2834, 1576, 1454,
1429, 1377, 1454, 1428, 1294, 1200, 1154, 1041, 938, 828, 772, 678, 605;
δH (400 MHz, CDCl3) 2.45 (6H, s, CH3), 3.70 (6H, s, OCH3), 6.10 (2H, d, J
2.0, Ar-H), 6.19 (1H, t, J 2.3, Ar-H), 7.16 - 7.26 (3H, m, Ar-H): δC (100
MHz, CDCl3) 21.8 (CH3), 55.2 (OCH3), 96.8 (Ar-CH), 103.5 (Ar-CH), 128.4
(Ar-CH), 129.5 (Ar-CH), 129.9 (Ar-C), 140.3 (Ar-C), 144.0 (Ar-C), 161.0
(Ar-C); m/z (EI) M, 274; (Found: M, 274.1017. C16H18O2S requires M,
274.1022).
