$DATUM 4-(4-Methylthiobenzoyl)quinazoline (4q). MeSNa (15% in water, 2 ml) was
added to a mixture of 4b (126 mg, 0.5 mg) in 1,4-dioxane (10 ml). The
mixture was refluxed overnight, and then cooled. The product was
extracted with ethyl acetate, washed with brine, and dried over Na2SO4.
The organic layer was evaporated and the residue was purified by silica
gel column chromatography (hexane/ ethyl acetate). 4q (118 mg, 84%) as a
yellow solid. 1H-NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 9.43 (1H, s), 8.17 (1H, d, J =
8.5 Hz), 8.08 (1H, d, J = 8.5 Hz), 8.01-7.98 (1H, m), 7.88 (2H, d, J =
8.5 Hz), 7.69-7.66 (1H, m), 7.30 (2H, d, J = 8.5 Hz), 2.54 (3H, s).
FAB-Mass: 281 (M+1).
