$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4,6-Bis(4-tert-butylmercaptophenyl)pyrimidine, 3e. A slurry of
4,6-bis-(4-fluorophenyl)pyrimidine 3d (1.26 g, 4.70 mmol) and sodium
tert-butylthiolate (1.16 g, 10.34 mmol) in DMF (25 mL) was heated at 70
°C for 18 h. Water (50 mL) was added to the reaction mixture, and the
solution was extracted with ether (1 × 150 mL, 2 × 50 mL). The combined
organic extracts were dried over MgSO4, filtered, and evaporated.
Recrystallization from ethanol gave fine, colorless needles (1.60 g,
84%): mp 151.5-152.5 °C; 1H NMR (CDCl3, 600.17 MHz) δ 9.29 (d, J = 1.2
Hz, 1H, 2-H), 8.09 (d, J = 1.2 Hz, 1H, 5-H), 8.08 (1/2AB, J = 8.4 Hz, 4H,
2'-H, 6'-H), 7.66 (1/2AB, J = 8.4 Hz, 4H, 3'-H, 5'-H), 1.31 (s, 18H,
C(CH3)3); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 150.91 MHz) δ 163.9 (C-4, C-6), 159.3 (C-2),
137.8 (C-2', C-6'), 137.2 and 136.6 (C-1' and C-4'), 127.2 (C-3', C-5'),
112.9 (C5), 46.6 (CMe3), 31.2 (CH3); IR (CH2Cl2) 2950m, 1575s, 1505s,
1450s, 1270s cm-1; MS (ES+) (%) 409 (100) (M + H)•+. Anal. (C24H28N2S2)
C, H, N.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
