$DATUM Synthesis of 2-(2-Bromophenylsulfanyl)benzaldehyde (5a):
2-Fluorobenzaldehyde (3; 2.0 g, 16 mmol), 2-bromo-thiophenol (4a; 3.0 g,
16 mmol) and anhyd K2CO3 (3.29 g, 23.8 mmol) were dissolved in MeCN (10
mL) and stirred at 100 °C for 30 min under MW conditions. The crude
reaction mixture was evaporated onto Celite and purified using column
chromatography on silica gel (eluent: heptane → 30% EtOAc in heptane).
Yield: (3.97 g, 84%); colorless solid. Rf 0.61 (EtOAc-heptane, 1:2); mp
49-50 °C. 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 10.39 (s, 1 H), 7.95 (dd, J=
7.6,1.7 Hz, 1 H), 7.66 (dd, J= 7.9,1.3 Hz, 1 H), 7.48-7.51 (m, 1 H), 7.43
(m, 1 H), 7.24-7.28 (m, 1 H), 7.14-7.21 (m, 3 H). 13C NMR (151 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = 191.8, 138.8, 135.7, 134.6,134.4, 133.6, 133.3, 131.8, 131.6,
129.3, 128.4, 127.5,126.4. GC-MS: m/z = 392 [M+]. Anal. Calcd for
C13H9BrOS: C, 53.26; H, 3.09. Found: C, 53.22; H, 3.05.
