$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3-(4'-Methoxyphenyl)sulfanylbenzoic acid (Table 2. entry 3): To a
round-bottom-flask were added 3-Bromobenzoic acid (402 mg, 2 mmol),
i-Pr2NEt (700 μL, 4 mmol), dry 1,4-dioxane (8.0 mL). The mixture was
evacuated and backfilled with nitrogen (3 cycles). Catalyst Pd2(dba)3 (46
mg, 0.05 mmol), Xantphos (58 mg, 0.1 mmol) and 4-methoxythiophenol (246
μL, 2 mmol) were added and then the mixture was degassed twice more. The
mixture was heated to reflux for 6 h and HPLC confirmed the completion of
the reaction. The reaction mixture was then allowed to reach ambient
temperature. The reaction mixture was acidified with acetic acid to reach
pH 3-4 then filtered and concentrated. The crude product was purified by
flash column chromatography on silica gel to afford the
3-(4-methoxyphenyl)sulfanylbenzoic acid (432 mg, 83% yield) as white
solid. Column chromatography solvent (hexane / ethyl acetate = 10 : 1).
Rf = 0.45 (hexane / ethyl acetate = 1 : 1). Melting point; 120-121 °C. 1H
NMR (CDCl3, 500 MHz) δ 7.89 (t, 1H, J = 1.6 Hz), 7.85 (dt, 1H, J = 8.8
Hz, 1.6 Hz), 7.45 (dt, 2H, J = 8.8 Hz, 2.1 Hz), 7.32-7.35 (m, 2H), 6.93
(dt, 2H, J = 8.8 Hz, 2.1 Hz), 3.84 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 125 MHz) δ
171.20, 160.28, 140.16, 135.95, 132.76, 129.97, 129.15, 129.00, 127.31,
122.99, 115.27, 55.40. IR (KBr, cm-1) 2964, 2943, 2902, 2875, 2856, 2840,
2813, 2360, 2342, 1688. HRMS m/z calcd for C14H12O3S 260.0507; Found,
260.0503.
