$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (2-nitro-phenyl)-phenyl ether (3a)
(2-nitro-phenyl)-(2,6-dichlorophenyl) sulfide (3j). Following above
procedure, 2,6-dichlorobenzenethiol (4.47g, 25mmol), KOH (1.40g, 25mmol)
and 1-chloro-2-nitro-benzene (3.94g, 25mmol) were used. 3j (7.47g) was
obtained as a yellow powder in 83% yield. 1H NMR (300MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.31
(dd, 1H, J = 1.5, 8.4 Hz, Ar-H); 7.26-7.55(m, 5H, Ar-H); 6.68 (dd, 1H, J
= 1.5, 8.4 Hz, Ar-H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and Characterization of Titanium(IV) Complexes Bearing
Monoanionic [O-NX] (X = O, S, Se) Tridentate Ligands and Their Behaviors
