$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative Procedure for the Synthesis of
4-Methoxyphenyl Phenyl Sulfide (Table 2, entry 2). An oven-dried 4 mL
vial containing a stirrer bar was charged with an 4-methoxyphenyl bromide
(93.5 mg, 0.5 mmol), catalyst (6.5 mg, 2 mol%) and KOtBu (84.2 mg, 0.75
mmol) in the glove box and sealed with a cap containing a PTFE / Silicone
septum. Toluene (1 mL) and thiophenyl (0.60 mmol) were injected
sequentially. The mixture was stirred at 100°C for 6 h. The crude was
purified by column chromatography on silica gel with petroleum ether as
eluent. Benzyl 4-chlorophenyl sulfide (Table 3, entry 9): silica gel
column chromatography (petroleum ether) gave 97.4 mg (0.42 mmol, 83%) of
the product as white solid. mp 57.6-58.4 °C. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ
7.28-7.23 (m, 5H), 7.20 (s, 4H), 4.07(s, 2H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ
137.1, 134.7, 132.4, 131.4, 128.9, 128.7, 128.5, 127.3, 39.3. EIMS m/z:
234 (M+)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, catalyst prepared and used, the article was retracted by
the corresponding author in "Synlett", 2014, 25(5),750
