$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure for Reaction of
2-Iodoanilines with Carbon Disulfide and Aliphatic Thiols. Amixtureof
K2CO3 (3.0mmol), thiol (1.2 mmol), and CS2 (1.2 mmol) in DMF (2.0 mL) was
stirred at rt for 1 h before CuBr (3.0mmol) and 2-iodoaniline (1.0 mmol)
were added. The resultant mixture was heated at 110 °C for 6 h.The cooled
solution was partitioned between ethyl acetate and water. The organic
layer was washed with water and brine and dried over Na2SO4. After
removal of solvent in vacuo, the residue was chromatographed to give the
corresponding benzothiazole. 2-(Cyclopentylthio)-6-nitrobenzo[d]thiazole
(13o). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.68 (d, J = 2.1 Hz, 1H), 8.30 (dd, J =
9.0 Hz, J = 2.1 Hz, 1H), 7.90 (d, J = 8.7 Hz, 1H), 4.24-4.12 (m, 1H),
2.45-2.26 (m, 2H), 1.92-1.65 (m, 6H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 174.8,
157.2, 143.9, 135.5, 121.8, 121.2, 117.3, 46.9, 33.7 (2C), 24.9 (2C);
ESI-MS m/z 281.0 (M + H)+; HRMS (EI) calcd for C12H12N2O2S2 (M+)
280.0340, found 280.0335.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of 2-thio-substituted benzothiazoles via a domino
condensation/S-arylation/heterocyclization process
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
