$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 9-[p-(Ethoxycarbonyl)phenylsulfanyl]triptycene
(2h). Under a nitrogen atmosphere, to a solution of sodium
9-triptycylthiolate in 28 mL of DMF, prepared from 9-triptycylthiol (6)34
(407 mg, 1.42 mmol) and sodium hydride (58 mg, 1.51 mmol), were added
p-(ethoxycarbonyl)iodobenzene (390 mg, 1.41 mmol) and copper(I) iodide
(27 mg, 1.38 mmol) at 70 °C. The mixture was stirred for 38 h at 110-115
°C and then poured into ice-cold water. Then, 2 mL of 36% hydrochloric
acid was added. The precipitate was separated by suction filtration and
extracted with 150 mL of benzene. The organic layer was washed with 25 mL
of a 28% aqueous solution of ammonia (×2) and 30 mL of water (×2) and
dried over sodium sulfate. The crude product was purified by column
chromatography (SiO2, benzene/hexane ) 3/1, v/v) and GPC and
recrystallized from dichloromethane and n-hexane. Compound 2h was
isolated in 47% yield as a colorless solid (286 mg):
9-(p-Cyanophenylsulfanyl)triptycene (2i). Following the method used for
the preparation of 2h, 2i was obtained in 83% yield as colorless solid mp
265.5-266.5 °C (from cyclohexane); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3/TMS) δ 5.47 (s,
1H), 6.96 (dt, J = 1.2, 7.5 Hz, 3H), 7.06 (dt, J = 0.9, 7.3 Hz, 3H), 7.20
(br d, J = 8.2 Hz, 2H), 7.40 (d, J = 7.3 Hz, 2H), 7.41 (d, J = 7.3 Hz,
3H) 7.45 (d, J = 6.9 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 53.9, 62.1,
107.9, 118.8, 123.3, 123.6, 125.0, 126.0, 128.3, 131.6, 142.0, 142.2,
145.1. Anal. Calcd. for C27H17NS, C, 83.69; H, 4.42; N, 3.61. Found: C,
83.98; H, 4.51; N, 3.61.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM reactant assumed
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Evidence for Effective p(Z)-π(Ar) Conjugations (Z = S, Se, and Te, as
Well as Z = O) in 9-(Arylchalcogenyl)triptycenes: Experimental and
Theoretical Investigations
