$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Synthesis of Aryl
Sulfides To a stirred solution of diaryliodonium tetrafluoroborate (1
mmol), Pd (PPh3)4 (58 mg, 5 mol%), Na2CO3 (106 mg, 2 mmol), and anhydrous
THF (5 mL) under nitrogen atmosphere was added mercaptan at room
temperature. The mixture was stirred at room temperature for an hour. The
solvent was evaporated off. To the residue, a saturated NH4Cl solution (5
mL) was added and then extracted with ether (2 x 10 mL). The organic
layer was dried over anhydrous MgSO4 and evaporated in vacuo. The crude
product was separated by preparative thin layer chromatography on silica
gel with hexane as a developer to afford the desired product, aryl
sulfide. 3-Nitrophenyl 4'-methylphenyl Sulfide (entry 8), yield 83%. M.p.
60°-61°C (Lit.21 m.p. 61°C) 1H NMR 7.10-8.10 (m,8H) 2.30 (s,3H) I.R.
3045, 2870, 1630, 1570, 1480, 1450, 1390, 1300, 1175, 1110, 1070, 1005,
900, 830, 790 cm-1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Hypervalent iodine in synthesis. 55. An efficient method for synthesis of
aryl sulfides by palladium-catalyzed reaction of hypervalent iodonium
salts with mercaptans
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Wang, Li; Chen, Zhen-Chu
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2001), 31(8), 1227-1232

