$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Anhyd DMSO (5 mL) was added to a mixture of
2-HSC6H4OH (151 mg, 1.2 mmol), 3,4-F2C6H3CN (139 mg, 1.0 mmol), and K2CO3
(345 mg, 2.5 mmol) under N2, and the mixture was stirred for 3 h at 60
°C. The mixture was then cooled to r.t. and extracted with EtOAc (3 × 25
mL). The organic layers were combined, washed with sat. brine (2 × 20
mL), dried (MgSO4), filtered, and concentrated under reduced pressure.
The crude product was purified by column chromatography [silica gel,
P-CH2Cl2 (2:1)]. Phenoxathiine-1-carbonitrile (4b), Yield: 187 mg (83%),
White solid. Reactant: 1-Halo-2-nitroarene 2b, Time: 3 h. m.p. 99.4-100.5
°C. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.00-7.03 (m, 1H), 7.04-7.10 (m, 1H),
7.13-7.22 (m, 4H), 7.33-7.36 (m, 1H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 110.53,
115.80, 117.71, 117.88, 121.75, 125.36, 125.89, 127.05, 127.80, 128.62,
128.82, 151.19, 152.58. HRMS (ESI, m/z): calcd for C13H8NOS [M+H]+
226.0321, found 226.0318. IR (film): 737, 1288, 1429, 1439, 2232 cm-1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Regioselective synthesis of phenoxathiin derivatives under
transition-metal-free conditions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Hu, Fangdong; Zhao, Xin; Li, Yanqiu; Feng, Lei; Ma, Chen
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2013), 45(7), 966-970

