$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of compounds 5-10 (general
procedure). An appropriate thiol (1 mmol) and Et3N (0.1 g, 1 mmol) were
added to a solution of 8-chloro-5,7-dinitroquinoline (4) (0.25 g, 1 mmol)
in dimethoxyethane (50 mL). The reaction mixture was stirred at room
temperature for 0.5-2 h until the starting compound was completely
consumed (monitoring by TLC) and poured into a 1 : 1 mixture of water and
HCl (250 mL). The precipitate that formed was filtered off, washed with
water to a neutral reaction, and dried in air. Oily products were
extracted with ethyl acetate (2×50 mL), and the extracts were dried with
Na2SO4 and concentrated. 8-(4-Chlorophenylthio)-5,7-dinitroquinoline (9).
Yield 0.21 g (83%), orange crystals. Temperature: 20 °C, time: 1 h. m.p.
150-152 °C (EtOH). Found (%): C, 49.67; H, 2.41; N, 11.67; S, 8.93.
C15H8ClN3O4S. Calculated (%): C, 49.80; H, 2.23; N, 11.62; S, 8.86. 1H
NMR (DMSO-d6), δ: 7.35 (s, 4 H, Ph); 7.96 (dd, 1 H, J1 = 8.8 Hz, J2 = 4.0
Hz); 8.86-9.02 (m, 2 H); 9.09 (d, 1 H, J = 2.7 Hz). 13C NMR (DMSO-d6), δ:
120.01, 121.75, 126.51, 129.26, 132.08, 132.41, 132.81, 137.74, 144.40,
145.78, 148.71, 152.72.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM 8-R-5,7-Dinitroquinolines in [3+2] cycloaddition reactions with
N-methylazomethine ylide
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Bastrakov, M. A.; Leonov, A. I.; Starosotnikov, A. M.; Fedyanin, I. V.;
Shevelev, S. A.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Russian Chemical Bulletin (2013), 62(4), 1052-1059

