$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-Bromo-4-acetyl-1-(m-tolylsulfinyl)benzene 1d A mixture of
1-bromo-2-fluoro-5-acetyl-benzene (0.8 g, 3.7 mmol), 3-methylbenzenethiol
(0.4 g, 3.6 mmol), K2CO3 (0.56 g, 4.1 mmol) in DMF (5 mL) was heated to
160 ◦C for 2 h in a closed vial. After cooling to ambient temperature the
mixture was diluted with diethyl ether (10 mL), washed (water, brine),
dried (MgSO4) and concentrated in vaccuo. The crude thioether was
directly oxidized. To a solution of the corresponding crude thio ether
(1.2 g, 3.6 mmol) in dichloromethane (60 mL) at 0 ◦C was added dropwise a
solution of m-CPBA (1.0 g, 60 %, 3.6 mmol) in dichloromethan (120 mL).
The reaction mixture was stirred at 0 ◦C for a period of 2 hours.
Standard workup followed by chromatography (solvent: c-hexane : ethyl
acetate = 1 : 2) afforded the pure sulfoxide 1d. yellow solid (1.0 g, 3.1
mmol, 83 % over two steps). 1H-NMR (CDCl3, 300MHz): δ= 8.17 (d, J =
8.0Hz, 1H), 8.11-8.06 (m, 2H), 7.58-7.53 (m, 2H), 7.35-7.25 (m, 2H), 2.60
(s, 3H), 2.36 (s, 3H) ppm. 13C-NMR (CDCl3, 75MHz): δ= 195.7, 149.9,
143.5, 140.1, 139.7, 132.8, 132.7, 129.1, 128.0, 126.5, 126.4, 123.6,
120.2, 26.7, 21.4 ppm. m. p.: 57 ◦C (iso-PrOH). MS (EI): m/z = 336.0,
338.0. IR (ATR): ev = 3078 (w), 1692 (s), 1377 (s), 1259 (s), 1228 (s),
1042 (s) cm-1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM closed vial used (stage 1); thioether isolated in stage 1 used crude in
stage 2; dropwise addition of mCPBA/CH2Cl2 (stage 2)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Palladium-Catalyzed Intramolecular Direct Arylation of 2-Bromo-diaryl
Sulfoxides via C-H Bond Activation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Wesch, Thomas; Berthelot-Brehier, Anais; Leroux, Frederic R.; Colobert,
Francoise
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2013), 15(10), 2490-2493

