$DATUM 3-tolyl-4'-tolylsulfide 3-Bromotoluene (2.04 mL, 16.81 mmol, 1.0 equiv),
2-propanol (17 mL), potassium hydroxide (2.18 g, 33.62 mmol, 2.0 equiv),
tetrakis (triphenylphosphine)palladium(0) (194 mg,, 0.168 mmol, 0.01
equiv), (S)-BINAP (209 mg, 0.336 mmol, 0.02 equiv) and pthiolcresol (2.0
mL, 16.81 mmol, 1.0 equiv) were heated under a nitrogen atmosphere for 4
h at 83 °C. After the reaction was completed it was cooled (<30 °C) and
quenched with water (17 mL) which resulted in formation of an oil. The
mixture was allowed to granulate for 1h at 10-15 °C. The slurry was
filtered, extracted and concentrated to dryness. Obtained a brown oil6,
2.99 g. 3-tolyl-4'-tolylsulfide, Yield 83% m/z 214; C14H14S requires: C,
78.45; H, 6.58; S, 15.0. Found: C, 78.1; H, 6.37; S, 15.3%; 1H NMR (300
MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 7.22 (m, 8H), 2.29 (s, 3H), 2.26 (s, 3H); IR (cm-1) νmax;
1591, 1491, 1475.
